{"uid":"cd08ba69e5b18ece","name":"test_publish_project_scoped_draft_requires_operator_scope_not_just_project_role","fullName":"tests.test_routes_openapi_integrations#test_publish_project_scoped_draft_requires_operator_scope_not_just_project_role","historyId":"4810daca0e388f6d36de2dbb4815fe99","time":{"start":1792437811066,"stop":1792437811145,"duration":79},"description":"GitHub Copilot review (round 2, PR #294): the project-scoped branch\n    of `publish_openapi_tool_draft` gained a `require_scopes(request,\n    [SCOPE_ADMIN, SCOPE_OPERATOR])` call, closing a gap where a project\n    owner/editor holding only the universal `caliber.viewer` scope could\n    still publish (`resource.publish` requires `caliber.operator` per\n    section 2.4). The existing publish test never exercises this because it\n    never sets a project on the integration at all -- this proves the\n    negative case directly with a real, project-scoped integration and a\n    real (non-admin) project editor.","descriptionHtml":"<p>GitHub Copilot review (round 2, PR #294): the project-scoped branch<br />\nof <code>publish_openapi_tool_draft</code> gained a <code>require_scopes(request, [SCOPE_ADMIN, SCOPE_OPERATOR])</code> call, closing a gap where a project<br />\nowner/editor holding only the universal <code>caliber.viewer</code> scope could<br />\nstill publish (<code>resource.publish</code> requires <code>caliber.operator</code> per<br />\nsection 2.4). The existing publish test never exercises this because it<br />\nnever sets a project on the integration at all -- this proves the<br />\nnegative case directly with a real, project-scoped integration and a<br />\nreal (non-admin) project editor.</p>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1792436381960,"stop":1792436381960,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters